      "card_ids": ["C03", "C17", "C18"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Structurally related ondansetron has absolute oral bioavailability of approximately 50–70% in humans across multiple records, supporting F ≥ 20% for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C01", "C05", "C07", "C11", "C14"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 records show that the closely related imidazobenzodiazepine ethyl ester XHE-III-74EE (M01) is stable in human and mouse liver microsomes and S9 fractions for 1 hour with a predicted half-life of several hours, supporting low hepatic first-pass for this chemotype.",
      "card_ids": ["C59", "C60", "C61", "C70"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "C68 shows ondansetron, alosetron and GR87442 have comparable hepatic clearances in human hepatocytes, consistent with ondansetron's high oral bioavailability; it does not provide a numeric clearance for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C68"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The physicochemical prior is favorable for oral absorption (MW 303 Da, logD 1.77, no HBD, neutral at physiological pH, moderate TPSA), supporting but not proving F ≥ 20%.",
      "card_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim": "No affirmative threshold-relevant evidence for F < 20% is present.",
      "card_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C59", "C60", "C61", "C70", "C68"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct flumazenil-specific oral bioavailability record is available; the decision relies on transfer from other molecules and a close analog.",
    "The only cirrhosis-matched record is for pentoxifylline, a structurally different xanthine; transferability to the imidazobenzodiazepine query is uncertain.",
    "No query-specific measured hepatic clearance, ester hydrolysis, permeability, or solubility data are supplied.",
    "The M01 analog differs from flumazenil (pyrrolidine/methoxy versus N-methyl/fluoro), so its excellent microsomal stability may not fully transfer.",
    "All available records are high-F; there is no affirmative low-F comparator to test the threshold."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high: the only cirrhosis-matched record (pentoxifylline F = 0.71 ± 0.24) and structurally related ondansetron records (F ≈ 50–70%) support F ≥ 20%, consistent with the favorable physicochemical prior; L6 adds supportive hepatic-stability evidence for a closely related imidazobenzodiazepine ethyl ester, and no affirmative low-F evidence is present."
}

